  "osmTag": "shop=bakery",
  "facts": [
   {
    "text": "Run by Mendoza, Argentina natives Elisa Cruz and Alejandra Príncipe.",
    "url": "https://www.islandernews.com/food/taste/b-bakery-from-mendoza-argentina-to-key-biscayne-with-authentic-flavors/article_ba93d58d-a501-49db-b9ef-e59980b8b40b.html"
   },
   {
    "text": "The business began in Mendoza in 2010 as a catering company and opened its first bakery there in 2018.",
    "url": "https://www.islandernews.com/food/taste/b-bakery-from-mendoza-argentina-to-key-biscayne-with-authentic-flavors/article_ba93d58d-a501-49db-b9ef-e59980b8b40b.html"
   },
   {
    "text": "The menu centers on medialunas, alfajores, savory sandwiches and coffee.",
    "url": "https://www.islandernews.com/food/taste/b-bakery-from-mendoza-argentina-to-key-biscayne-with-authentic-flavors/article_ba93d58d-a501-49db-b9ef-e59980b8b40b.html"
   },
   {
    "text": "Took the place of the island bakery Clásica Victoria, which was sold and rebranded as Bë Bakery.",
    "url": "https://www.islandernews.com/food/taste/optimism-for-2026-high-with-local-restaurateurs/article_7198459d-583e-4ae8-9ea5-d7fd37b875c2.html"
   }
  ]
 },
